AI Master Tutor & Training Agent:-
An advanced, locally-hosted AI tutor and conversational agent built with Python. This project utilizes local Large Language Models (LLMs) via Ollama and LangChain to provide an interactive educational experience without relying on cloud APIs. It features a modern web interface built with Streamlit and a backend API powered by FastAPI. 
🌟 Key Features:-
Dual Operation Modes: Users can select between "💬 Casual Chat" for friendly conversations or "📚 Study Masterclass" for structured educational deep dives.  Structured Learning Paths: In Masterclass mode, the AI breaks topics down into Beginner, Intermediate, and Advanced levels.  Comprehensive Generation: Generates study schedules, detailed explanations with bullet points and code blocks, and multiple-choice quizzes (MCQs) for assessment.  Downloadable Study Materials: Users can generate and download their "Main Study Notes" and "MCQ Quiz Books" as Markdown (.md) files.  Session Management: Integrates an SQLite database to automatically save, load, and delete chat histories and study sessions.  Multilingual Support: Supports output in multiple languages, including English, Odia, Hindi, Bengali, and Spanish.  Theme Customization: Includes a toggle for Light ☀️ and Dark 🌙 UI themes.  FastAPI Backend: Provides API endpoints (e.g., /get-plan) to programmatically generate training plans.
🛠️ Technology Stack:-
Language: Python 3.11 / 3.13
Frontend UI: Streamlit
Backend API: FastAPI, Uvicorn 
AI Engine: LangChain (ChatOllama) 
Database: SQLite (sqlite3) 
Containerization: Docker  
📋 Prerequisites:-
Before running this project, ensure you have the following installed:Python: Version 3.11 or higher.  Ollama: You must have Ollama installed and running on your local machine to process the AI requests.  Local Models: Pull the required models using your terminal:ollama run llama3.2:1b (Used for the fast Streamlit UI)  ollama run llama3 (Used for the FastAPI backend)
🚀 Installation & Setup:-
1. Clone the repository and navigate to the project directory.
2. Create and activate a virtual environment:Bashpython -m venv .venv
(Note: Use .venv\Scripts\activate on Windows or source .venv/bin/activate on macOS/Linux).  
3. Install the required dependencies:Bashpip install fastapi uvicorn langchain-community streamlit pysqlite3
  💻 UsageThis project consists of two main entry points: the graphical user interface and the API.Running the Streamlit Web UITo launch the interactive AI Master Tutor interface, run:Bashstreamlit run app.py
  
Note for Windows users: The app.py file includes a built-in asyncio.WindowsSelectorEventLoopPolicy() fix to prevent ConnectionResetError (WinError 10054) when the server reloads.
Running the FastAPI BackendTo launch the API server, run:Bashuvicorn main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000
  
You can then access the API at http://localhost:8000/get-plan?topic=your_topic&level=your_level.  
🐳 Docker SupportA Dockerfile is included for easy containerization.To build and run the Docker
image:Bashdocker build -t ai-training-agent .
docker run -p 8000:8000 ai-training-agent
